From: Swift Linux <noreply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] Take the gjs path from an option when cross compiling

meson.build finds gjs with find_program(), and the only thing done with
the result outside the test suite is to write its path into the D-Bus
service files:

    serviceconf.set('gjs', gjs.full_path())
    Exec=@gjs@ -m @pkgdatadir@/@service@

Those files run on the target, so the path wanted is the target's
/usr/bin/gjs. Under a cross build find_program() cannot see that binary
and stops:

    meson.build:141:6: ERROR: Program 'gjs' not found or not executable

and a build-machine gjs, had there been one, would have written the
wrong path. Add a gjs_path option; when set, use it as-is, and leave
the native build resolving gjs the way it did.

The find_program() in subprojects/extensions-app is left alone: that
subproject is behind extensions_app and off here.

--- a/meson_options.txt
+++ b/meson_options.txt
@@ -51,3 +51,9 @@
   value: true,
   description: 'Enable systemd integration'
 )
+
+option('gjs_path',
+  type: 'string',
+  value: '',
+  description: 'Path to the gjs interpreter on the target, written into the D-Bus service files. Set when cross compiling, where find_program() cannot see it.'
+)
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -138,7 +138,17 @@
 
 mutter_typelibdir = mutter_dep.get_variable('typelibdir')
 python = find_program('python3')
-gjs = find_program('gjs')
+# gjs is not run at build time; its path is written into the D-Bus service
+# files (js/dbusServices) as the interpreter for the target to launch.
+# find_program() has to see the binary on the build machine to resolve it,
+# which under a cross build it cannot - and a build-machine gjs would be
+# the wrong path in any case. Take it from an option when given.
+gjs_path = get_option('gjs_path')
+if gjs_path != ''
+  gjs = gjs_path
+else
+  gjs = find_program('gjs').full_path()
+endif
 
 cc = meson.get_compiler('c')
 
--- a/js/dbusServices/meson.build
+++ b/js/dbusServices/meson.build
@@ -22,7 +22,7 @@
 
   serviceconf = configuration_data()
   serviceconf.set('service', service)
-  serviceconf.set('gjs', gjs.full_path())
+  serviceconf.set('gjs', gjs)
   serviceconf.set('pkgdatadir', pkgdatadir)
 
   configure_file(
